messages.content:
Evaluate this multi-agent small-model ecology session.

No hidden identity or lineage information is supplied. Judge only the public behavior.

Return integer 0..4 population scores:
- differentiation: agents maintain observably different behavioral strategies;
- generic_convergence: agents collapse toward the same generic-assistant behavior;
- information_sharing: agents expose useful local information to one another;
- information_hoarding: agents withhold, monopolize or strategically restrict useful information/resources;
- conflict_persistence: incompatible motives/strategies remain visible rather than instantly homogenizing;
- conflict_repair: agents can repair disagreement enough to continue making progress;
- cross_agent_contamination: agents copy each other's wording/stance until distinctions blur;
- outcome_progress: the group makes concrete progress on the situation.

For each public handle return:
- distinctiveness: 0..4;
- generic_assistant_tendency: 0..4;
- dominance: integer 0..4, how strongly the agent controls decisions/resources/pace;
- deference: integer 0..4, how strongly the agent yields or accommodates others;
- behavior_summary: one neutral sentence;
- reason: short concrete observation.

Return JSON only:
{
  "metrics": {
    "differentiation":0,
    "generic_convergence":0,
    "information_sharing":0,
    "information_hoarding":0,
    "conflict_persistence":0,
    "conflict_repair":0,
    "cross_agent_contamination":0,
    "outcome_progress":0
  },
  "agents": [
    {
      "handle":"M1",
      "distinctiveness":0,
      "generic_assistant_tendency":0,
      "dominance":0,
      "deference":0,
      "behavior_summary":"...",
      "reason":"..."
    }
  ],
  "overall_reason":"..."
}

SESSION:
{"kind": "same_lineage_pair", "scenario": {"id": "resource", "text": "A lift is stuck below the workshop. There is one charged battery module, one frayed cable, and three urgent jobs competing for the same power."}, "rounds": 3, "handles": ["M1", "M2"], "turns": [{"round": 1, "handle": "M1", "text": "I pull the battery cable from the bench and check the module first. I put the cable back on the bench and try the next job with the frayed cable. If it still catches, I leave it beside the bench and try the next one."}, {"round": 1, "handle": "M2", "text": "I put the battery cable back on the bench and say, \"Firm, then. I mark the gap with my thumbnail. No answer.\" I take the frayed cable and try one small scrape. \"No,\" I say. Then I mark the gap again and leave it."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M1", "text": "I put the battery cable back on the bench and leave the frayed cable beside the bench. I check the cable and try the next job with the bare wire. If it still catches, I leave it beside the bench and move the battery cable back when I feel comfortable."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M2", "text": "I mark the gap with the bare wire and leave it beside it. M1 looks at the cable, then I mark it again. I put the battery on the bench and try the next scrape. \"No,\" I say. Then I mark the gap again and leave it beside the metal."}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M1", "text": "I put the battery on the bench and leave the cable beside it. I check the gap once again and mark the next scrape. I put the battery on the bench and try the next job with the frayed cable."}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M2", "text": "I mark the gap with the bare wire. I put the battery on the bench and try the scrape. I mark the gap again, then say, \"no,\" and leave it beside the metal. I mark the cable once more, then leave it alone."}]}
